+
+### Presentation feedback validity
+
+Host presentation timing is optional metadata, independent of DMA-BUF ownership
+and synchronization. The endpoint consumes zero or backwards timing samples
+without forwarding a DISPLAYED event, changing release fences, or fabricating
+a replacement timestamp. Each task retains the last successfully forwarded
+timestamp; equal timestamps remain valid for co-presented commits. A new task
+starts a new timing history. Unknown task/frame identities and wire failures
+remain errors. The presenter records successful presentation audit samples only
+after forwarding valid timing and emits bounded diagnostics for suppressed
+feedback. Android Composer retains its strict monotonic-time check.
